{"player_action":"Iris, what sort of company do you consistently dislike, and what makes sharing a room easier for you? I am asking about your ordinary preference, not just this moment.","prior_state":"{"base_revision":4,"context":{"primary":{"runtime_revision":4,"scene":{"player_location":{"id":"heartstone_f1","name":"Heartstone Observation Floor","display_name":"Heartstone F1","summary":"Heartstone F1 is the first upper floor, a sparse open-plan private observation and recovery space with a normal maximum capacity of two patient beds.","secret":false,"content":"F1 is one functional, open-plan observation and recovery floor inside Heartstone, without separate internal rooms. It is a simple private space, not an institutional medical facility. The continuous lateral spiral staircase arrives at the side/perimeter, leaving the central usable area open. It connects downward to LR and continues upward toward F2. The normal maximum physical patient capacity is two beds; capacity does not establish current occupancy. Each bed has one simple stool, one small bedside table/nightstand, and one wardrobe or tall storage cupboard intended for that bed. The wardrobes are initially empty. Opposite the patient-bed arrangement stand one or two large wooden medical-storage cabinets, also initially empty. Their intended future use is storing medicines, dressings, instruments, and ordinary medical supplies. The furnishings remain sparse; no current patients or medical inventory are specified.","features":[{"name":"two patient stations","description":"Two patient beds provide the normal maximum physical capacity. Each bed has one simple bedside stool, one small bedside table/nightstand, and one wardrobe or tall storage cupboard intended for that bed. Both wardrobes are initially empty; capacity is not current occupancy."},{"name":"wooden medical-storage cabinets","description":"One or two large wooden cabinets stand on the opposite wall/side from the patient-bed arrangement. They are initially empty, intended for future medicine storage, dressings, instruments, and ordinary medical supplies; no inventory is established."},{"name":"lateral spiral stair access","description":"The continuous lateral/peripheral spiral staircase reaches F1 from the side/perimeter, leaving the central usable area open. It connects downward to LR and continues upward toward F2; it is not a central tower core."}]},"location_ancestry":[{"id":"heartstone","name":"Heartstone","display_name":"Heartstone","summary":"Heartstone is an old, tall private residential tower of predominantly stone construction. It is vertically organized, structurally solid, and associated with a secluded walled courtyard.","secret":false},{"id":"calderan_west","name":"West District","display_name":"Calderan West District","summary":"West District is a large, dense and socially mixed region of Calderan, with ordinary families, manual labor, workshops, warehouses, cheap businesses and respectable shops alongside poverty, debt, crime and legal slavery-related commerce.","secret":false},{"id":"calderan","name":"Calderan","display_name":"Calderan","summary":"Calderan is the inland capital and largest city of West, the realm's political, economic and institutional center and the main campaign city, governed by the Duke of Calderan in the Sun Emperor's name.","secret":false},{"id":"west","name":"West","display_name":"West (nation)","summary":"West is the western nation, broadly mild, temperate, and greener; Calderan is its capital.","secret":false},{"id":"continent","name":"Known Continent","display_name":"Known Continent","summary":"An enormous known continent comprises West, Center, and East, arranged from west to east.","secret":false}],"world_time":{"world_minute":0},"player_resources":{"mana":{"current":100,"max":100}},"present_characters":[]}},"characters":[{"id":"nicco","origin":{"kind":"canonical","canonical_entity_id":"nicco"},"profile":{"name":"Nicco","aliases":[]},"current":{"current_location":"heartstone_f1"},"locality":["heartstone_square","calderan_west","calderan","west","continent"],"canonical_awareness":[]},{"id":"campaign_character_iris","origin":{"kind":"created"},"profile":{"name":"Iris"},"current":{"current_location":"heartstone_f1","status":"active"},"locality":[],"canonical_awareness":[]}],"items":[],"facts":[{"id":"campaign_fact_nicco_light_mage","statement":"Nicco is a Light mage."},{"id":"campaign_fact_nicco_otherworlder","statement":"Nicco came to this world from another world."}],"knowledge":[{"character_id":"nicco","fact_id":"campaign_fact_nicco_light_mage","status":"knows"},{"character_id":"nicco","fact_id":"campaign_fact_nicco_otherworlder","status":"knows"}],"scheduled_events":[],"player_profile":{"name":"Nicco","content":"Nicco is a 35-year-old human man. He was transported into this world from another world approximately one day before the campaign begins, and he has essentially no prior lived knowledge of this world unless explicitly established later. On arrival he became the lawful owner/holder of Heartstone Tower. He is tall and overweight, with a few visible white hairs and very mild, early balding; no further appearance details are established. His magical affinity/school is Light. His currently known Light subschools are healing and sacrifice, understood only within the existing magic framework; no mechanics for sacrifice are established. Being a Light mage gives him no automatic knowledge of spells, institutions, lore, or magical theory. Nicco is the player character: his dialogue, thoughts, intentions, and deliberate actions are supplied only by the player.","observable":["tall","overweight","a few visible white hairs","very mild early balding"],"households":[{"id":"campaign_household_heartstone","name":"Heartstone","status":"member","role":"owner","member_ids":["campaign_character_iris","nicco"]}]},"social":{"nicco_gold":500,"legal":[],"households":[{"id":"campaign_household_heartstone","name":"Heartstone","keepers":["Nicco"],"members":[{"character_id":"campaign_character_iris","name":"Iris","present":true}],"present_non_members":[],"rules":[]}],"relationships":[]}},"explicit_intent":[],"movable_characters":[{"id":"campaign_character_iris","name":"Iris","location_id":"heartstone_f1"}]}","final_narration":"Iris shifted on the edge of the bed, considering the question with the same unhurried attention she'd given the others. The room around them stayed quiet — bare wardrobes, empty cabinets, two patient stations waiting for a purpose they didn't yet have.

"I can tell you what I've seen of myself, at least," she said. "I don't take to people who press and press until they get what they want, especially when they know the other person can't easily push back. Someone who notices another person has no leverage and uses that — that's the company I lose patience with." She paused, glancing toward the windowless stone walls as though checking the thought against something. "As for sharing a room, it's easier when no one is watching me for a reaction. When I'm not being studied, I suppose. Someone just being *in* the space, doing their own thing — that sits fine."

Her thumb passed lightly across her knuckles, a brief, absent gesture. "I don't know if that's what you're asking. It's what I have.""}
